V(n-1) }\n\nwhere:\n\n- V(n) is the value of the optimal solution at stage n\n- c is the cost vector\n- x(n) is the decision variable at stage n\n- V(n-1) is the value of the optimal solution at stage n-1\n\nThis recursive definition allows us to break down the problem into smaller sub-problems, solve each sub-problem, and then combine the solutions to obtain the value of the optimal solution for the original problem.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The value of the optimal solution is recursively defined as the maximum value of the optimal solution to the subproblems of the problem, obtained by considering each possible choice of action at each decision point.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The value of the optimal solution can be defined recursively as follows:\n\n- For a problem with no variables (i.e., a problem with no decision to be made), the value of the optimal solution is the optimal objective function value.\n- For a problem with one or more variables, the value of the optimal solution is the maximum (or minimum, depending on the problem type) of the values of the optimal solutions of the subproblems obtained by fixing one variable at a time.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The value of the optimal solution can be defined recursively as follows:\n\n- If the problem has no more sub-problems (i.e., it is a base case), then the value of the optimal solution is the value of the optimal solution to this base case.\n- Otherwise, consider the optimal solutions to the sub-problems, and for each one, recursively find the value of the optimal solution.\n- Choose the value of the optimal solution that maximizes/minimizes the objective function (depending on whether the problem is a maximization or minimization problem).\n\nMathematically, this can be represented as:\n\n`V(x) = max/min { f(x) + V(x1), f(x) + V(x2),..., f(x) + V(xn) }`\n\nwhere:\n- `V(x)` is the value of the optimal solution to the problem\n- `f(x)` is the objective function\n- `x1, x2,..., xn` are the sub-problems\n- `V(x1), V(x2),..., V(xn)` are the values of the optimal solutions to the sub-problems\n\nThis recursive definition is the core idea behind dynamic programming, which is a method for solving complex problems by breaking them down into simpler sub-problems and solving each sub-problem only once.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The value of the optimal solution can be defined recursively as follows:\n\nLet's consider a problem with a set of decisions `D` and a set of states `S`. The value of the optimal solution at a given state `s` is denoted as `V(s)`.\n\n**Recursive Definition:**\n\n`V(s) = max_{d in D(s)} [R(s, d) + γ * V(next_state(s, d))]`\n\nwhere:\n\n- `D(s)` is the set of decisions available at state `s`.\n- `R(s, d)` is the reward obtained by taking decision `d` at state `s`.\n- `next_state(s, d)` is the next state reached by taking decision `d` at state `s`.\n- `γ` is the discount factor (0 <= γ <= 1), which represents the importance of future rewards.\n\nThis recursive definition states that the value of the optimal solution at state `s` is the maximum value of the rewards obtained by taking each decision `d` at state `s`, plus the discounted value of the optimal solution at the next state `next_state(s, d)`.\n\nThis recursive definition can be applied to each state in the problem, until the value of the optimal solution is computed for all states."}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The value of the optimal solution is the maximum value of the values of the optimal solutions of its subproblems.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The value of the optimal solution is the maximum value of the optimal solution for its subproblems.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: It originated in a smart information retrieval system.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: It was initially incorporated in a smart information retrieval system.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The concept was first implemented in a smart information retrieval system.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The concept was initially implemented in a smart information retrieval system.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: The system was used in smart information retrieval.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input senten