['<s>The essence of a sentence is often captured by its main subjects and actions, while descriptive terms provide additional but less central details. With this in mind , this sentence : "i remained under the banyan tree , exhausted by my daily ritual of dragooning the men every two hours ." means in one word:"', '<s>The essence of a sentence is often captured by its main subjects and actions, while descriptive terms provide additional but less central details. With this in mind , this sentence : "I stayed under the banyan tree, exhausted from my daily routine of forcing the men to work every two hours." means in one word:"', '<s>The essence of a sentence is often captured by its main subjects and actions, while descriptive terms provide additional but less central details. With this in mind , this sentence : "I stayed under the banyan tree, drained by coercing the men every two hours repeatedly daily." means in one word:"', '<s>The essence of a sentence is often captured by its main subjects and actions, while descriptive terms provide additional but less central details. With this in mind , this sentence : "Exhausted from my daily routine, I remained under the shade of the banyan tree." means in one word:"', '<s>The essence of a sentence is often captured by its main subjects and actions, while descriptive terms provide additional but less central details. With this in mind , this sentence : "Exhausted, I had been under a banyan tree, repeatedly gathering men every 2 hours." means in one word:"'] 10674
